{
	title: 'System-prompt change trail in the transcript',
	spec: 'When a file in a session\'s system prompt (SYSTEM.md, the files it includes, the AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md files for its cwd) changes, the session gets an output record with the change: file name (relative to the cwd when inside it), changed/added/removed, and a short diff (git diff -U1, headers dropped, at most 40 lines). The prompt-file watcher (task 48) runs the check for every open tab when it sees a save, and at host start for edits made while it was down; the first check of a session only remembers (state in the session\'s prompt-files.json), and files that come or go with a cwd change are not reported. The model reads each record as a <meta> note in front of its next prompt, saying the user edited its instructions and earlier replies followed the old text, with the diff, so it does not mistake new rules for ones it ignored. Clients show consecutive change records as one card: one change heads as \'SYSTEM.md changed\'; several as \'3 changes to SYSTEM.md, AGENTS.md since 10:44\' (a date before the time if not today). Both clients draw it alike, without a header: one change is one row ("11:25 AGENTS.md changed  +2 −0") with up to three changed lines in diff colors, or "blank lines only"; a run is one row ("11:14–11:25 3 changes to SYSTEM.md, AGENTS.md"; one time when first and last match) and one aligned row per change: time, file, counts, its first changed line. A change that removes and adds words shows instead every changed span with a word of context ("Apply Strunk → Prunk & …", "−Foo Pull …", "… end +now"): context dim, removed words in the remove color struck through, added words in the add color. Its removed and added lines are compared as two runs of words, so a rewrapped paragraph or several edits across hunks show only the changed words; beyond one line for another, a change keeping under half its removed words is a rewrite and shows its first changed line. Only the changed text takes diff colors: time, file and counts stay dim, and a removed line is struck through, never the whole row. The web card opens on a click to each change\'s line and whole diff, in the same colors.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Records are output records with a change field (no new record type): replay turns them into notes, transcript.aside carries change, and promptChanges.group merges runs at draw time in both clients (web view.rows, terminal frame.layout), memoized per run so keyed rows and the terminal layout cache keep the object.',
		"Web: an opened change's diff lines stay whole and scroll sideways as one box, right edge fading, like a wide markdown table; only the collapsed summary rows are cut with an ellipsis. Truncated diff lines on a phone hid the change itself.",
		'A multi-line edit used to show only its first changed line; a removed first line struck the whole row, time and file included, so an edit read as a deletion. Invariant: an edit shows its changed words, and the row lead never takes diff colors.',
		"Prompt-file change cards open and close in both clients by /toggle and Ctrl-O too (common toggle.toggles), closed at first; the terminal's open card adds each change's line and whole diff, like the web. A merged run folds under its first block number.",
		'Bug fix (2026-10-09): text a plugin adds to or removes from the system prompt (around systemPrompt.assemble) was never reported. Invariant restored: every change to the prompt the model gets reaches the session, plugin-made ones included. prompt-trail records the lines plugins add (and removed ones, marked) as a pseudo-file plugins/, by comparing the hooked prompt with the unhooked original; prompt-files re-checks open tabs when the assemble hooks change.'
